{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1448375-altering-the-initiative-system","id":1448375,"title":"Altering the initiative system","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-12T18:54:10-07:00","id":1448375,"title":"Altering the initiative system","content":"I've got a party of experienced role-players enjoying Mage for the first time, and the only real hitch for the players is the initiative system, It's hard for people used to other systems to do the declaring their actions from lowest to highest, then doing the rolls, then storytelling the action. I'd like to make them more comfortable by using a more traditional init system and honestly, I know I could try to teach these players the WoD way but honestly it's likely they would then just drift back to other games. <br /> <br /> Borrowing from v5e, I'm thinking ordering actions descending:<ul><li>Anyone want to cast a spell w/out using focus (off the cuff, very hard magic to do without any &quot;components&quot;)</li> <li>Anyone doing short range/melee attacks</li> <li>Anyone entering melee range and attacking</li> <li>Anyone doing long range attacks</li> <li>Anyone casting with focus? (you gotta wave your arms, say words, etc.. based on your focus/paradigm/insturments)</li> <li>Anyone doing anything non-combat? (disarming the bomb, flipping the switch that everyone is fighting over not being switched, etc...)</li> <li>Finally, anyone have any supernatural &quot;extra&quot; actions like using the Time sphere or fast vamps/werewolves.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> If two people act in the same action group above, they would then compare Dex + Wits, and if necessary role.<br /> <br /> If you plan on splitting your dice-pool (I'm doing two things, like jumping the car over the bridge, AND shooting the pistol out the window), you get to act at the lower of the two (driving would be non-combat). You still have to choose the least sized dice pull (are you a worst shot or a worst driver? You choose the one you are crappier at), and then choose how many dice to put to each activity. Say you shoot with 8 dice, but drive with only 5, in that example. You take the 5 dice, then decide to split them: say 2 dice toward driving, and 3 for shooting.<br /> <br /> Another consideration is dodging/blocking. In m20 you can use your action to dodge/block. If you go first in init, and want to change your previous action to dodge/block, you need to make a willpower role to explain why you changed the course of your turn to dodge/block. This gets strange when you go to v5e style init system. I'm thinking about giving people one free dodge/block a turn to compensate, but that seems like it would unbalance the system, making it more &quot;pulp mode&quot;<br /> <br /> What am I missing while considering this alteration? Other possible gotchas like Dodge/block?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26830-mogmismo","name":"mogmismo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T15:02:42-07:00","id":1448471,"title":"","content":"Mage properly reflects the fragility of the human body where guns are concerned. Long ranged attacks, which is the only category into which firing guns fits neatly, is fourth in order. First in order is anyone Not using their focus and casting Magick. The player who does this will have a better chance of doing something to stop an enemy firing on them or another player. Casting Magick with focus might never happen, because it is fifth in order. Players are going to learn very quickly to ditch their foci.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to reward players for learning the Magick System and their Tradition/Convention's foci, you could switch the fourth and fifth action-types.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T16:12:34-07:00","id":1448475,"title":"","content":"It also creates all sorts of weird questions regarding things like &quot;does firing a Wonder that does a ranged magical attack,&quot; count as 4th order (making a ranged attack) or 5th order (casting magic with Focus since you need to activate the Wonder)? If you've already case a Correspondence based effect that lets you punch people through portals, does that fall under 2nd order (short range attacks since they're punches), 3rd order (closing the distance to attack magically), or 4th order (ranged attacks despite them being your fists)?<br /> <br /> I think with freeform magic this sort of priority based initiative is going to end up with a lot of headaches.<br /> <br /> It's probably easier to either use a more traditional approach (just drop the declaration phase, highest init goes first, coupled with a passive base defense that can be boosted if you dedicate an action to it), or just going with one of the many newer approaches like the various &quot;popcorn&quot; initiative systems (Players and the ST pick the new character to act, which might be divided by &quot;sides&quot; or for everyone in combat) which help focus on teamwork by making two or three PC actions in a row get maximum impact without waiting for the end of the round to pull it off, but also you need to be conscious of tactics of breaking up PC and NPC actions vs. lots going in a row.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T09:29:31-07:00","id":1448516,"title":"","content":"Thank you both for your input. I'm still working this through, and this really helps<br /> <br /> Hoirizon Party:<br /> <br /> I'm with you on switching up the order, some good insights. Ditching your foci does come with disadvantages, even if you could act first, though. Probably not enough to dissuade players from wanting to go first. They don't have to go through all the process of using the foci, which seems faster, actually kind of instinctive, which is how I imagine they *first* do magic w/out a focus, and then are amazed about not needing them.<br /> <br /> Heavy Arms:<br /> <br /> I actually love popcorn initiative, in systems like Fate Accelerated. I'm curious about ideas about ideas around &quot;passive base defense&quot;. My first stab at that would be half your dodge/block pool (rounded down), usable at any time it's not your turn and added to dice for soaking as desired. If you actively block/dodge on your action, until your next action you get that 1/2 pool + a full dodge/block pool to add to any soak roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26830-mogmismo","name":"mogmismo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T11:17:27-07:00","id":1448524,"title":"","content":"I will admit that a truly passive static defense is probably a bit more house rules than just modifying initiative. The importance of some sort of passive defense is that in traditional &quot;roll high, go first,&quot; style initiative is the WoD actively declared defenses means that if you roll high, go first, and have no idea what everyone else is doing, you're actually in a shit situation regarding trying to figure out how much to put into offense and how much into defense. Knowing that you can attack, and have some defense, makes going first good instead of bad (as you can't abort to defense if you already used up your action to attack).<br /> <br /> So you could call it more a reflexive defense and just give everyone one free defensive roll per round. You could go full V5 and allow multiple defensive rolls that get cumulative penalties (you'd want to make this worse than the current full defense action though).<br /> <br /> Half of your applicable defensive roll is probably a bit high for a static passive value. With 1s subtracting successes, diff 6 is actually less than half on average. But it also doesn't take difficulty modifiers into account (something a lot of STs and players forget is a thing on defense, or choose to ignore for speed). You might want to pull from the CofD and do something like the lower of Dex or Wits for the Attribute part of things to lower the value a bit, and then have any difficulty mods to defense apply inversely to the attacker. So if I'm using magic to lower my Brawl rolls by -2, rather than trying to adjust my static defense, just switch it to a +2 difficulty to the attack.<br /> <br /> It's not perfect, but it's hard to make something smoother without redoing a lot more of the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T07:04:11-07:00","id":1448773,"title":"","content":"I'm going to go with Popcorn initiative, and some form of passive defense, as well as the ability to take a &quot;total defense&quot; action to boost the defense pool dramatically. I'll report back after a couple of sessions, and continue to be interested in how others have altered the m20 init system in their games.<br /> <br /> Also, as a new member of the forums here, I want to say I'm very impressed with the deep amount of thought and time that people put into replying to posts. It feels like a good community. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26830-mogmismo","name":"mogmismo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}